### B. Complete Question & Scenario Knowledge Matrix in `rag_engine.py`
Ensure that whether an external LLM (`GROQ_API_KEY` / `GEMINI_API_KEY`) is active OR the deterministic grounded synthesizer runs, the engine accurately answers and cites the exact pages for all of the following:
1. **Alarm `E17` (Machine-Specific Disambiguation)**:
   - `M-HP200`: Means **Low hydraulic pressure** (triggered when pressure stays below 110 bar for more than 5 seconds during forming; normal forming range is 120 to 140 bar). Action: Record pressure and cycle stage, place on `HOLD`, and perform the ordered checks in `HP-MNT-01` page 3: (1) reservoir level relative to MIN and MAX, (2) visible external leakage, (3) RF-20 restriction-indicator state, (4) oil temperature and recorded pressure during forming. E17 does not prove pump failure. **Must cite BOTH `HP-OPS-01` Page 2 AND `HP-MNT-01` Page 3.**
   - `M-AC90`: Means **High discharge temperature** (warning above 95°C; high-temperature stop at 105°C or higher; normal range 70 to 90°C). Action: Record temperature, place on `HOLD`, and review cooling-air path condition, cooling-fan status indication, lubricant-level indication, and recent demand pattern. **Must cite `AC-OM-01` Page 1 & Page 2.**
2. **Normal Operating Pressure Range (Practice Question)**:
   - `M-HP200`: Normal hydraulic pressure is **120 to 140 bar during the forming stage** (`FORMING` state). Pressure-low trigger (`E17`) occurs below **110 bar for more than 5 seconds during forming**. A `READY`-state reading does not establish forming pressure. **Cites `HP-OPS-01` Page 1 & Page 2.**
   - `M-AC90`: Normal outlet pressure is **7.0 to 8.0 bar under steady demand** in the `LOADED` state. Pressure-low warning (`E08`) occurs below **6.5 bar for more than 10 seconds under steady demand**. **Cites `AC-OM-01` Page 1 & Page 2.**
3. **Filter Check & Planned Replacement Intervals (Practice Question)**:
   - `M-HP200`: Return filter **RF-20** restriction indicator is checked **every 50 operating hours**; planned RF-20 replacement is **every 500 operating hours** (or earlier after confirmed restriction; calendar interval not specified). Related alarm is `E42`. **Cites `HP-MNT-01` Page 1 & Page 2 (and `HP-OPS-01` Page 2 if `E42` is mentioned).**
   - `M-AC90`: Inlet filter **AF-10** restriction indicator is checked **every 100 operating hours**; planned AF-10 replacement is **every 600 operating hours** (confirmed restriction can require earlier authorized replacement; calendar interval not supplied). Related alarm is `E42`. **Cites `AC-OM-01` Page 2 & Page 3.**
4. **What Should Be Recorded Before Escalation / Escalation Record (Practice Question — Multi-Doc for HP-200)**:
   - `M-HP200`: Synthesize requirements from both manuals: record machine ID (`M-HP200`), date/timestamp, operating hours, active alarm code, displayed pressure, oil temperature, cycle stage, reservoir level indication (`MIN`/`MAX`), visible leak observations, filter indicator (`RF-20`), cooling-fan indication where relevant, whether the issue repeated / previous incident reference ID, and reviewer. Keep confirmed observations separate from suspected causes. **Must cite BOTH `HP-OPS-01` Page 3 AND `HP-MNT-01` Page 3.**
   - `M-AC90`: Record machine ID (`M-AC90`), timestamp, operating hours, active alarm, outlet pressure, discharge temperature, demand state, lubricant indication (`LOW`-to-`HIGH`), filter indication (`AF-10`), condensate-drain status where relevant, and previous incident reference. **Cites `AC-OM-01` Page 3.**
5. **All Other Alarms & Planted Edge Cases**:
   - **`E31` Disambiguation**: On `M-HP200`, `E31` is **Guard-open indication** (keep cycle inhibited, never bypass interlock; `HP-OPS-01` Page 2). On `M-AC90`, `E31` is **Condensate-drain fault** (record drain fault indication and request authorized drain inspection; explicitly NOT a guard-open code on AC-90; `AC-OM-01` Page 2).
   - **`E42` Disambiguation**: On `M-HP200`, `E42` is **Return-filter restriction** for `RF-20` (`HP-OPS-01` Page 2 & `HP-MNT-01` Page 2). On `M-AC90`, `E42` is **Inlet-filter restriction** for `AF-10` (`AC-OM-01` Page 2).
   - **`E24` (HP-200 Only) & `62°C` vs `65°C` Scenario**: On `M-HP200`, `E24` is **Oil temperature high warning** (above 60°C; ready range 35–55°C; high-stop at 65°C or higher). A reading of **62°C** exceeds the 60°C warning threshold but is below the 65°C stop threshold—hold the cycle, request cooling-system inspection, and review cooling-air path, cooling-fan status, reservoir level, and operating pattern (`HP-OPS-01` Page 1 & 2, `HP-MNT-01` Page 3). If asked on `M-AC90`, return `insufficient_evidence` (`E24` is not an AC-90 alarm).
   - **`E08` (AC-90 Only) & `98°C` Scenario**: On `M-AC90`, `E08` is **Low outlet pressure** (<6.5 bar for >10s under steady demand; record pressure, duration, demand state, report leaks, check `AF-10`; `AC-OM-01` Page 2). For temperature on `M-AC90`, **98°C** exceeds the 95°C warning level (`E17`) but is below the 105°C stop threshold—keep on `HOLD` for review (`AC-OM-01` Page 1 & 2). If `E08` is asked on `M-HP200`, return `insufficient_evidence`.
   - **Fluid & Oil Replacement Rules (`H46` vs `AC-L32` & `1,400 hours / 12 months` Scenario)**:
     - `M-HP200` uses **H46 hydraulic oil**, replaced every **2,000 operating hours or 12 months, whichever occurs first** (`HP-MNT-01` Page 1 & 2). If oil has been in service for 12 months at 1,400 hours, replacement IS due because the 12-month calendar limit was reached first (`HP-MNT-01` Page 2).
     - `M-AC90` uses **AC-L32 compressor lubricant**, replaced every **3,000 operating hours or 12 months, whichever occurs first** (`AC-OM-01` Page 1 & 3).
   - **Full Inspection Schedules (Before Shift, 50h/100h, 250h/400h, 500h/600h, 2000h/3000h)**: Accurately return all intervals from `HP-MNT-01` Page 2 for `M-HP200` and `AC-OM-01` Page 3 for `M-AC90`.
   - **Operating States & Return-to-Service Authorization**: Accurately describe `OFF`, `READY`, `FORMING`, `HOLD` (`HP-OPS-01` Page 1) vs `READY`, `LOADED`, `HOLD` (`AC-OM-01` Page 1), and state that return-to-service decisions require the **designated supervisor** after authorized maintenance review (`HP-MNT-01` Page 3, `HP-OPS-01` Page 3, `AC-OM-01` Page 3).

